module

public import Rule30Open.Columns.TwelveCells

/-!
# Fourteen cells: absorption for every right half that is white past its first fourteen cells

Every right half of at most fourteen cells, driven by a word of period four from any phase, enters the kit's
ether-and-wall family, as [TwelveCells](TwelveCells.md) shows for twelve. So every right half whose cells `15 .. G` are
white enters, whatever its first fourteen cells and whatever lies beyond `G`, with `G = 750`, `1446` and `560` for
`0001`, `0011` and `0111` (`fourteen_0001`, `fourteen_0011`, `fourteen_0111`), and no finite configuration with such a
right half has a center column that repeats the word (`fourteenRight_0001`, `fourteenRight_0011`,
`fourteenRight_0111`). In particular no finite configuration whose right half has at most fourteen cells does
(`smallFourteen_0001`, `smallFourteen_0011`, `smallFourteen_0111`).

The entries come from `computations/small_halves.py`, 128 halves to a kernel check (`halvesOK` of TenCells), and
`chunks_cover` of TwelveCells gathers the 128 chunks of each word and phase.

The natural-language argument is `FourteenCells.md`, beside this file.
-/

@[expose] public section

-- Sequential elaboration: the kernel checks would otherwise run in parallel and stack their memory.
set_option Elab.async false

namespace Rule30Open

open Ruliology.CellularAutomata
open Rule30Jen Rule30Realization Rule30Ether Rule30StripCertificates Rule30PeriodTwoSideways

/-- **Absorption across a white gap after fourteen cells.** If every right half below `2 ^ 14` has a passing entry,
every right half whose cells `15 .. G` are white enters the family, whatever lies beyond `G`. -/
theorem fourteen_absorption {w : List Bool} {A : List (Nat × Nat)} {φ G : Nat}
    (hcheck : ∀ r, r < 2 ^ 14 → ∃ t k, entryOK w A φ G r t k = true)
    (x : Nat → Bool) (hx : ∀ p, 14 < p → p ≤ G → x p = false) :
    ∃ a ∈ A, ∃ t1, InFamily (drv (fun t => wordAt w (t + φ)) x) a.1 (a.2 + φ) t1 := by
  obtain ⟨r, hr, hxr⟩ := pack_gap 14 G x hx
  obtain ⟨t, k, hok⟩ := hcheck r hr
  obtain ⟨hG, a, ha, hf⟩ := entryOK_spec hok
  exact ⟨a, ha, t, inFamily_of_fast hf fun q h1 h2 => hxr q h1 (by omega)⟩

